WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.748 --> 00:00:01.929
Yikes! [s@Yikes!

2
00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:03.790
Who are you?

3
00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.753
I'm an American alligator.

4
00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:12.197
Alligators are large reptiles.

5
00:00:14.278 --> 00:00:15.299
Where do you live?

6
00:00:28.532 --> 00:00:30.514
We live in the United States.

7
00:00:32.556 --> 00:00:33.977
We like warm water.

8
00:00:35.699 --> 00:00:38.621
We swim in rivers, lakes, and swamps.

9
00:00:40.823 --> 00:00:42.005
What do you eat?

10
00:00:43.706 --> 00:00:47.510
We like frogs, fish, snails, and mammals.

11
00:00:48.791 --> 00:00:50.592
Alligators don't chew food.

12
00:00:52.614 --> 00:00:54.296
We just gulp it down!

13
00:00:58.996 --> 00:01:01.058
You have wide jaws.

14
00:01:02.639 --> 00:01:04.561
My jaws are very strong.

15
00:01:06.922 --> 00:01:09.344
I can even crack a turtle's hard shell!

16
00:01:12.327 --> 00:01:14.629
We grab prey with our sharp teeth.

17
00:01:18.231 --> 00:01:20.233
This swamp is noisy!

18
00:01:21.994 --> 00:01:23.756
Alligators hiss loudly.

19
00:01:27.064 --> 00:01:29.325
We can roar like lions too.

20
00:01:34.028 --> 00:01:35.329
Do you hibernate?

21
00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.991
No. But we sleep in holes sometimes.

22
00:01:41.632 --> 00:01:43.593
We find a muddy spot in water.

23
00:01:45.595 --> 00:01:47.736
Then we dig holes to keep warm.

24
00:01:49.857 --> 00:01:51.878
Your tail looks powerful!

25
00:01:53.919 --> 00:01:54.940
It is powerful.

26
00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.081
My tail moves me through the water.

27
00:02:01.203 --> 00:02:02.523
I love to swim.

28
00:02:06.946 --> 00:02:07.807
I'm getting hungry.

29
00:02:10.148 --> 00:02:16.472
Bye. See you later, American Alligator!
